# HB Briefing - Watchlist
#
# Promote any subject to a fixed category and status, regardless of keyword scoring.
# One rule per line:
#
#     match phrase [& phrase] | category | status [| note]
#
# - Every phrase joined with "&" must appear, at a word start, in the item's title
#   or summary. "metronet & bbb" therefore needs both.
# - category: regulatory_action, litigation, billing_dispute, equipment_scam,
#   deceptive_fees, data_breach, security, policy, other
# - status (severity): high, medium, low
# - Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the first match wins, so put the
#   highest-priority matter first. Lines starting with # are ignored.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ your own identifiers
# Add whoever or whatever you must never miss. Listed first so they win every tie.
# Example:
# acme telecom | regulatory_action | high | the company you track
# jane doe | other | high | principal

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ MetroNet: always top
# KKR-backed fibre operator; every mention is escalation-grade by request.
# Narrower rules go first because the first match wins.
metronet & better business bureau | billing_dispute | high | BBB complaints about MetroNet
metronet & bbb | billing_dispute | high | BBB complaints about MetroNet
metronet | regulatory_action | high | MetroNet - always highest significance

# --------------------------------------------------------- related parties and regulators
kkr | regulatory_action | medium | investor
iowa attorney general | regulatory_action | high | state regulator
fcc | regulatory_action | medium | federal regulator
federal communications commission | regulatory_action | medium | federal regulator
